1. Explain the difference between frontend, backend, and full-stack        
      development with suitable real-world examples.
Ans:-1. Frontend Development:- Frontend development focuses on the part of a website or application that users directly interact with — the user interface (UI).
Technologies used:
HTML (structure)


CSS (styling)


JavaScript (interactivity)


Frameworks/Libraries: React, Angular, Vue.js
2. Backend Development
Backend development handles the server-side logic, database, and application functionality — things that users don’t see but make the app work.
Technologies used:
Languages: Node.js, Python (Django, Flask), Java (Spring Boot), PHP


Databases: MySQL, MongoDB, PostgreSQL




3. Full-Stack Development
 Full-stack developers work on both frontend and backend, meaning they can build an entire web application from start to finish.
Technologies used:
Frontend + Backend tools


Example stacks: MERN (MongoDB, Express.js, React, Node.js), MEAN (MongoDB, Express.js, Angular, Node.js)


