3. Describe how a browser requests and displays a web page from a web server.
When you type a website address in your browser and press Enter, the browser first contacts a DNS server to find the IP address of that website. Then it connects to the web server using HTTP or HTTPS and sends a request for the web page. The server processes the request and sends back the page’s files (like HTML, CSS, and JavaScript). The browser receives these files, builds the page, applies styles, runs scripts, and finally displays the complete webpage on your screen.
