6. Define the roles of a frontend developer, backend developer, and database administrator in a project.
Ans-A frontend developer is responsible for creating the part of a website that users see and interact with. They design and build the user interface using HTML, CSS, and JavaScript to make the website look attractive, responsive, and easy to use. 
A backend developer works on the server side of the website. They handle the logic, process user requests, connect to databases, and ensure smooth communication between the frontend and the server using languages like Python, Node.js, or Java.
 The database administrator manages and maintains the database that stores all the website’s data. They make sure the data is organized, secure, and regularly backed up so that the website functions properly and information is always available when needed.
